      ro: "Acest important oraș comercial din nord este adesea considerat centrul istoric al zonei Varendra. Astfel, locul se numără printre punctele caracteristice ale Bangladeshului, în Delta Gange-Brahmaputra, pe Golful Bengal și în apropierea pădurilor de mangrove Sundarbans, și oferă o imagine asupra culturii bengaleze, a musonului și a identității regionale. Este situat în statul sud-asiatic Bangladesh. Regiunea este definită de Delta Gange-Brahmaputra și Golful Bengal. Climatul este de tip muson tropical, cu sezon ploios și sezon secetos pronunțate.",
      en: "Bogra, often referred to as the 'Capital of North Bengal,' is an ancient city located on the banks of the Karatoya River. It is one of the oldest cities in Bangladesh and serves as a major commercial and transport hub for the northern region. Bogra is most famous for its proximity to Mahasthangarh, the earliest urban archaeological site in the country, which was the capital of the Pundra Kingdom. The city is also renowned for its unique 'Bogra Doi' (sweet yogurt), a delicacy that is famous throughout the country. Historically, Bogra has been a center for trade, agriculture, and industry, particularly in light engineering and agricultural machinery. The city's vibrant markets and its role as a gateway to the northern districts make it a vital economic center. Bogra also boasts several historic mosques and colonial-era buildings. History K8 — Ancient Capitals and Northern Trade."
