      en: "Kushtia, situated on the banks of the Gorai River, is widely recognized as the cultural capital of Bangladesh. It is most famous for its association with the great mystic poet and philosopher Lalon Shah, whose shrine (Lalon Akhra) attracts thousands of followers and tourists every year. Kushtia was also a major center for the activities of the Nobel laureate Rabindranath Tagore, whose ancestral estate, the Kuthibari at Shilaidaha, is located nearby. Historically, the city flourished as a center for trade and industry during the British era, particularly with the establishment of textile mills and the railway. Today, Kushtia remains a hub for education, traditional music, and literature. The city's serene landscape and its deep-rooted connection to the Baul tradition make it a unique destination for those seeking spiritual and cultural enrichment. Geography K7 — Cultural Landscapes and Mystic Traditions."
